            "title": "Tilray isn't sacrificing efficiency on its beer brands, CEO says",
            "description": "<p>Tilray Brands (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TLRY\">TLRY</a>) stock is fired up on Thursday, up nearly 25% after the cannabis company beat fiscal first quarter estimates: revenue of $210 million (vs. estimates of $205 million) and flat adjusted earnings of $0.00 per share (vs. estimates of a loss of $0.03). The company also owns and operates a variety of cannabis products and alcohol brands, including a handful of breweries.</p>\n<p>Tilray Brands Chairman and CEO Irwin Simon comments on Tilray's beverage operations and its cost-saving strategies over the years that have maintained efficiency.</p>\n<p>Also read up on Yahoo Finance's interview with Constellation Brands (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/STZ\">STZ</a>) CEO Bill Newlands, who speaks on <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/constellation-brands-ceo-says-the-modelo-maker-is-feeling-the-squeeze-from-softer-economy-fewer-drinkers-172616650.html\">navigating the tough consumer environment</a> for his company's beer brands.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "Tilray Brands (TLRY) stock is fired up on Thursday, up nearly 25% after the cannabis company beat fiscal first quarter estimates: revenue of $210 million (vs. estimates of $205 million) and flat adjusted earnings of $0.00 per share (vs. estimates of a loss of $0.03). The company also owns and operates a variety of cannabis products and alcohol brands, including a handful of breweries. Tilray Brands Chairman and CEO Irwin Simon comments on Tilray's beverage operations and its cost-saving strategies over the years that have maintained efficiency. Also read up on Yahoo Finance's interview with Constellation Brands (STZ) CEO Bill Newlands, who speaks on navigating the tough consumer environment for his company's beer brands. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more&nbsp;Market Catalysts.",
